message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
title: "Selective Prediction with Calibrated Uncertainty for Diabetic Retinopathy Screening: A Single-Backbone Benchmark on APTOS 2019"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-06-13"
authors:
  - family-names: "Khan"
    given-names: "Muhammad Shahnawaz"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4055-6563"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
    email: "shahnawaz.jrw@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ShahnawazKakarh/retinal-selective-prediction"
url: "https://github.com/ShahnawazKakarh/retinal-selective-prediction"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  We provide an open-source, single-backbone, single-seed,
  fully reproducible benchmark of four post-hoc uncertainty
  quantification methods on the APTOS 2019 diabetic
  retinopathy grading task. The release evaluates plain
  softmax confidence, Temperature Scaling, MC Dropout (T=30)
  with four uncertainty signals including BALD mutual
  information, and Split Conformal Prediction (with APS
  variant). All methods reuse a single trained EfficientNet-B0
  checkpoint and a single locked random seed. Results show
  that Temperature Scaling reduces Expected Calibration Error
  from 0.146 to 0.055, MC Dropout with mutual information
  yields the lowest AURC (0.0756), and Split Conformal hits
  empirical coverage 0.902 against a 0.90 target. The work
  is positioned as a reproducible benchmark rather than a
  novel methodological contribution; novel pieces and
  external validation are scoped for v1.1.0 and v2.0.0.
keywords:
